<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the full Menshykau & Iber (2013) GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Schnakenberg receptor-ligand reaction-diffusion equations, steady-state flux cancellation, linearized Turing dispersion curve, and 2D (a, b) Turing instability phase space (L111-249); solves the curved ureteric ampulla cap PDE via an unconditionally stable spectral cosine IMEX solver across rho_tip = pi*R_tip/lambda_c demonstrating exact m = 1, 2, 3, 4 hotspot transitions (L256-367); and couples 2D self-avoiding ureteric tree arborization to a 2D mesenchymal GDNF consumption sink field across WT, Gdnf+/- / PRR^(UB-/-) hypoplasia, Spry1-/- hyper-branching, and exogenous GDNF bead perturbations plus equal-diffusion and no-sink negative controls (L374-575). Backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 `sorry`s) in `Loop_054_kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L772-855) reports 8 quantitative morphometrics with reference values, dispersion statistics (RMSE, Pearson r, p-value, SD, CV), and negative-control ablation deltas: critical Turing wavelength lambda_c = 0.472569, 4/4 exact ampulla tip-splitting mode transitions ([1, 2, 3, 4] peaks), E11.0-E13.5 WT tip progression Pearson r = 0.9993 (p = 1.9e-8, Horton-Strahler R_b = 2.00 vs 2.04 reference), generational bifurcation angle RMSE = 3.86 deg (vs collapsed angles in no-sink ablation), Spry1-/- hyper-branch ratio = 1.875x, Gdnf+/- hypoplasia reduction ratio = 0.375x (-62.5%), and exact specimen tip counts (12 WT vs 6 mutant, ratio = 2.00x)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
